Subject: [PATCH 1043/1044] SableOS: Browser keys follow the design's T/B/L and
 add tab keys

Resolve the conflict between the first Browser key model and
BROWSER_WEBVIEW_UX: single keys now mean what the design gives them
in page and reader mode, and the address bar and new tab move to
their chords only.

* Single keys (only after the page declined the key, never while a
  form, the address bar or find has focus): T top, B bottom, L next
  link and Shift+L previous link (link mode), R reader mode, F or /
  find, Space and Shift+Space one block down and up, Move Home/End
  top and bottom. L no longer focuses the address bar, T no longer
  opens a tab and B no longer goes back.
* Chords (Alt on the Q25, Ctrl on an external keyboard): Alt+L
  address, Alt+T new tab, Alt+W close tab, Alt+K / Alt+J next /
  previous tab (also Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab), Alt+A tab grid,
  Alt+F find, Alt+R reload, Alt+Left/Right back/forward.
* tabGrid(): D, Del or Alt+W close the focused tab in the grid.
* adjacentTab(): next/previous tab in opening order, wrapping.
* hint(): the command dock hint line for start page, page and reader.

Pure Java; host tests in the SableOS Q25 repository
(tests/java/stock-apps/Jelly). Wired up by the next patch.
